WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:19.931
<v Host>Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June sixteenth. On the evening of the sixteenth, a strong earthquake hit the Kanto region near Tokyo. Two prefectures felt a level five-weak quake, but there was no danger of a tsunami. Let's listen.

00:00:20.532 --> 00:00:23.292
<v News>今日のニュースです。

00:00:23.992 --> 00:00:30.544
<v News>16日の夜、関東地方で大きな地震がありました。

00:00:31.243 --> 00:00:39.595
<v News>午後7時46分ごろ、茨城県の南部を震源とする地震が起きました。

00:00:40.295 --> 00:00:47.591
<v News>群馬県と埼玉県では、最大で震度5弱を観測しました。

00:00:48.292 --> 00:00:53.859
<v News>強い揺れで、棚から物が落ちた家もありました。

00:00:54.560 --> 00:01:00.896
<v News>地震の大きさを表すマグニチュードは、5.5でした。

00:01:01.595 --> 00:01:06.444
<v News>この地震による津波の心配はありません。

00:01:07.144 --> 00:01:14.512
<v News>今のところ、大きなけがや、建物の被害は報告されていません。

00:01:15.212 --> 00:01:24.043
<v News>気象庁は、これから1週間ほど、強い地震に注意するように呼びかけています。

00:01:24.743 --> 00:01:31.200
<v News>揺れの強かった地域の人は、安全に気をつけてください。

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.531
<v Host>Let's break it down.

00:01:34.132 --> 00:01:41.620
<v Slow>16日の夜、関東地方で大きな地震がありました。

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:47.123
<v Host>On the evening of the sixteenth, there was a big earthquake in the Kanto region.

00:01:47.724 --> 00:01:49.956
<v Vocab>地震

00:01:50.355 --> 00:01:58.203
<v Host>It means earthquake. The first character means earth or ground, the second means to shake — the ground shaking.

00:01:58.804 --> 00:02:08.331
<v Slow>午後7時46分ごろ、茨城県の南部を震源とする地震が起きました。

00:02:09.132 --> 00:02:16.836
<v Host>At around seven forty-six in the evening, an earthquake occurred with its epicenter in southern Ibaraki Prefecture.

00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:19.788
<v Vocab>震源

00:02:20.187 --> 00:02:28.611
<v Host>It means the epicenter — the underground point where an earthquake begins. The first character is quake, the second is source.

00:02:29.211 --> 00:02:37.539
<v Slow>群馬県と埼玉県では、最大で震度5弱を観測しました。

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:44.627
<v Host>In Gunma and Saitama Prefectures, they measured a maximum of level five-weak.

00:02:45.228 --> 00:02:47.460
<v Vocab>震度

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:59.692
<v Host>It means seismic intensity — how strongly the ground shakes at a place, on Japan's zero-to-seven scale. Don't confuse it with magnitude, which is the size of the quake itself.

00:03:00.292 --> 00:03:06.651
<v Slow>強い揺れで、棚から物が落ちた家もありました。

00:03:07.451 --> 00:03:11.987
<v Host>With the strong shaking, in some homes things fell off the shelves.

00:03:12.587 --> 00:03:14.532
<v Vocab>揺れ

00:03:14.931 --> 00:03:22.324
<v Host>It means shaking or a tremor. It's the noun from the verb to sway, to shake — the motion you actually feel.

00:03:22.924 --> 00:03:28.443
<v Slow>この地震による津波の心配はありません。

00:03:29.243 --> 00:03:32.651
<v Host>There is no danger of a tsunami from this earthquake.

00:03:33.252 --> 00:03:35.412
<v Vocab>津波

00:03:35.812 --> 00:03:44.883
<v Host>It means tsunami — a giant sea wave that an undersea quake can cause. It's already an English word, borrowed straight from Japanese.

00:03:45.484 --> 00:03:53.883
<v Slow>今のところ、大きなけがや、建物の被害は報告されていません。

00:03:54.683 --> 00:03:59.939
<v Host>So far, no serious injuries or damage to buildings have been reported.

00:04:00.539 --> 00:04:02.651
<v Vocab>被害

00:04:03.051 --> 00:04:13.084
<v Host>It means damage or harm — the loss caused by a disaster or accident. You'll hear it constantly in news about storms, floods, and quakes.

00:04:13.683 --> 00:04:23.788
<v Slow>気象庁は、これから1週間ほど、強い地震に注意するように呼びかけています。

00:04:24.588 --> 00:04:30.540
<v Host>The Meteorological Agency is urging people to watch out for strong earthquakes for about a week.

00:04:31.139 --> 00:04:33.732
<v Vocab>呼びかける

00:04:34.132 --> 00:04:45.028
<v Host>It means to call on people, to urge — to publicly ask everyone to do something. It literally combines to call and to hang, like sending a call out to the crowd.

00:04:45.627 --> 00:04:53.019
<v Slow>揺れの強かった地域の人は、安全に気をつけてください。

00:04:53.819 --> 00:04:58.379
<v Host>People in areas with strong shaking, please take care to stay safe.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:01.139
<v Vocab>安全

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:11.644
<v Host>It means safety, or safe. The opposite is danger. It works as a noun and as a describing word — a safe place, or simply safety.

00:05:12.244 --> 00:05:15.244
<v Host>Let's listen to the full story one more time.

00:05:15.843 --> 00:05:18.603
<v News>今日のニュースです。

00:05:19.303 --> 00:05:25.855
<v News>16日の夜、関東地方で大きな地震がありました。

00:05:26.555 --> 00:05:34.908
<v News>午後7時46分ごろ、茨城県の南部を震源とする地震が起きました。

00:05:35.608 --> 00:05:42.903
<v News>群馬県と埼玉県では、最大で震度5弱を観測しました。

00:05:43.603 --> 00:05:49.172
<v News>強い揺れで、棚から物が落ちた家もありました。

00:05:49.872 --> 00:05:56.208
<v News>地震の大きさを表すマグニチュードは、5.5でした。

00:05:56.908 --> 00:06:01.755
<v News>この地震による津波の心配はありません。

00:06:02.456 --> 00:06:09.824
<v News>今のところ、大きなけがや、建物の被害は報告されていません。

00:06:10.524 --> 00:06:19.355
<v News>気象庁は、これから1週間ほど、強い地震に注意するように呼びかけています。

00:06:20.055 --> 00:06:26.512
<v News>揺れの強かった地域の人は、安全に気をつけてください。

00:06:27.211 --> 00:06:29.947
<v Host>Quiz time. Three questions.

00:06:30.548 --> 00:06:36.163
<v Slow>地震があったのは、何日の夜でしたか。

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:41.019
<v Host>On the evening of which day was the earthquake? The sixteenth.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:50.500
<v Slow>群馬県と埼玉県では、最大でどのくらいの震度を観測しましたか。

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:57.516
<v Host>What was the maximum seismic intensity measured in Gunma and Saitama? Level five-weak.

00:06:58.115 --> 00:07:04.139
<v Slow>この地震で、津波の心配はありましたか。

00:07:04.939 --> 00:07:09.692
<v Host>Was there any danger of a tsunami from this quake? No, there was none.

00:07:10.291 --> 00:07:22.675
<v Host>That's today's Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

00:07:23.276 --> 00:07:25.531
<v News>また明日。
